  "visualBrief": "Individual Ghazanchetsots Cathedral in the photographed2018–2019 exterior: pale ashlar main body with three faceted entrance porches, round recessed portals, tall arched glazing, cross-shaped gable lights, crossing roof folds and faceted drum carrying a tall silver metal cone/cross. Separate western three-stage bell tower has a true open base passage, two arcaded levels and a peaked stone cone/cross. Shared ashlar/limestone/standing-seam metal/wood; metric UVs/linear tints. Mapped main/bell controls and standard viewer terrain. Exact sculpture, inscriptions, small carving/stained glass, surveyed paving/landscaping, later restoration changes, full interiors and certified walking excluded.",
